Modern Software Engineer Learning Areas

1. Core Software Engineering (Primary Skill)
   - System design
   - APIs and microservices
   - Databases
   - Clean code and testing
   - Distributed systems

2. Cloud (Must Have)
   - AWS / Azure / GCP fundamentals
   - IAM and access control
   - Containers (Docker)
   - Kubernetes
   - Infrastructure as Code (Terraform)
   - Monitoring and observability

3. AI (Increasingly Important)
   - LLM fundamentals
   - Prompt engineering
   - RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)
   - AI agents
   - Model evaluation
   - Fine-tuning basics
   - AI application development

4. Security (Essential for Everyone)
   Application Security:
   - OWASP Top 10
   - Authentication (OAuth, OIDC)
   - Authorization (RBAC)
   - Input validation
   - Secure coding practices

   Cloud Security:
   - IAM and least privilege
   - Secret management
   - Encryption
   - Network security
   - Secure cloud configurations

   AI Security:
   - Prompt injection
   - Jailbreak attacks
   - Data leakage prevention
   - RAG security
   - Tool-calling security
   - AI governance

Key Takeaway:
Today's high-value engineer is not just a coder. They can:
- Build software
- Deploy and operate it in the cloud
- Integrate AI capabilities
- Think about security from day one

Suggested Learning Focus:
40% Software Engineering
25% Cloud
25% AI
10% Security

Goal:
Build systems that are Functional + Scalable + Reliable + Secure + AI-enabled.


