Being a great engineer is more than being a great coder.

A good coder writes code that works.

A good engineer:
- Understands the business problem
- Designs robust systems
- Writes maintainable code
- Thinks about scalability and reliability
- Understands data and infrastructure
- Deploys and operates systems in production
- Considers security from the start
- Uses cloud services effectively
- Leverages AI where appropriate
- Balances trade-offs and makes sound technical decisions

Coding is only one part of engineering.

The real value of an engineer is the ability to design, build, deploy, operate, secure, and evolve systems that solve real-world problems.
